Supreme People's Court

Notice on Strictly Enforcing the Disciplinary Provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China

Fa Fa [2003] No. 5

To all local people's courts at various levels, all military courts of various levels, all railway transport intermediate courts and basic courts, all maritime courts, and all courts of the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps:

To thoroughly implement the spirit of the Second Plenary Session of the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, unswervingly continue to advance the construction of party conduct and integrity in the people's courts, and better provide strong judicial guarantees for comprehensively building a moderately prosperous society, the Supreme People's Court requires that all courts in the country must further seriously study and strictly enforce the disciplinary provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China, and vigorously strengthen the construction of power supervision systems and disciplinary constraint mechanisms.

1. Fully recognize the necessity of strict discipline. Strict discipline of the judges' ranks is not only necessary for building a high-quality contingent of judges but also a guarantee for judicial work to achieve fairness and justice throughout society. To promote the professionalization of judges and build a contingent of judges who are politically firm, professionally proficient, have fine conduct, and are judicially impartial, strengthening the power supervision system and disciplinary constraint mechanism is the key. The disciplinary provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China are the basic law for strengthening internal court supervision and constraining and regulating the professional conduct of judges. All judges must strictly abide by them. Courts at all levels must, in light of the higher requirements of the new situation for the judges' contingent, strengthen education, improve mechanisms, strictly manage the contingent in accordance with the law and discipline, and treat anti-corruption as a long-term task, consistently grasping it firmly and well.

2. All judges must effectively enhance their self-discipline awareness, using strict legal discipline to restrain and regulate their professional conduct. The lofty status and judicial authority of judges in society stem from the noble character shaped by strict disciplinary constraints. Article 32 of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China is the basic precept that every judge must strictly observe and is a basic requirement for the profession of judge. Every judge should strictly demand themselves accordingly, achieving self-discipline and self-vigilance, doubly cherishing the lofty profession of judge, and correctly exercising the power of adjudication.

3. Improve the inspection and supervision mechanism, and make every effort to ensure implementation. The Judges Law of the People's Republic of China is a constitutional-type law with a lofty status. Courts at all levels must, in light of actual conditions, establish and perfect relevant rules and regulations and ensure their implementation. Higher-level courts must strengthen inspection and supervision, make the implementation of discipline an important part of team building, study it as a special topic, and inspect it regularly; discipline inspection and supervision departments must take measures, come up with plans, and intensify efforts to ensure that the disciplinary provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China play an important role in the integrity construction of courts.

4. Strengthen the leadership responsibility system, grasping each level. Ensuring the integrity construction of the court contingent is an important duty of court leaders. Courts at all levels must, in accordance with the requirements of the Central Committee's provisions on implementing the responsibility system for party conduct and integrity construction, perfect the "dual responsibilities" system. They must incorporate the implementation of the disciplinary provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China as an important part of the "party conduct and integrity construction responsibility letter," integrate it into the target management of leading bodies and leading cadres, grasp it level by level, and ensure implementation at each level, so that leaders of courts at all levels effectively assume responsibility for integrity construction.

5. Intensify efforts and seriously investigate and punish illegal and disciplinary cases. Courts at all levels must adhere to the principle of addressing both symptoms and root causes and comprehensive governance, both preventing and treating illegal and disciplinary acts at the source and curbing the occurrence of such acts through resolute investigation and punishment of cases that have already occurred. For those who violate the disciplinary provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China, there must be no leniency or accommodation; they must be investigated thoroughly and dealt with seriously. If their acts constitute a crime, criminal liability must be determined resolutely. Through strict legal disciplinary accountability, the judges' contingent must be purified and its integrity maintained.

6. This notice applies to other staff of the court.

The above notice is to be earnestly implemented. Major issues shall be promptly reported to the Supreme People's Court.

February 27, 2003

Appendix:

Disciplinary Provisions of the Judges Law of the People's Republic of China

Chapter XI: Discipline

Article 32: A judge shall not commit any of the following acts:

(1) Spreading opinions that damage the reputation of the state, joining illegal organizations, participating in assemblies, processions, demonstrations, or other activities aimed at opposing the state, participating in strikes;

(2) Engaging in corruption or accepting bribes;

(3) Engaging in favoritism for personal gain and perverting the law;

(4) Extorting confessions by torture;

(5) Concealing or falsifying evidence;

(6) Divulging state secrets or secrets of judicial work;

(7) Abusing power to infringe upon the lawful rights and interests of natural persons, legal persons, or other organizations;

(8) Dereliction of duty, causing erroneous judgments or causing serious losses to the parties;

(9) Delaying handling of cases or causing delays in work;

(10) Using one's position to seek personal gain for oneself or others;

(11) Engaging in for-profit business activities;

(12) Meeting privately with parties or their agents, or accepting meals or gifts from parties or their agents;

(13) Other illegal or disciplinary acts.

Article 33: A judge who commits any of the acts listed in Article 32 of this Law shall be given a sanction; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be pursued in accordance with the law.

Article 34: Sanctions include: warning, demerit recording, major demerit recording, demotion, removal from post, and expulsion.

A person subject to removal from post shall also have their salary and rank reduced.

Article 35: The authority and procedures for imposing sanctions shall be handled in accordance with relevant provisions.
